WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.237
A plain timestamp stores a local date and time without time-zone interpretation.

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:07.907
A timestamptz represents an instant.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:12.882
If data crosses regions, plain local timestamps can become ambiguous.

00:00:12.882 --> 00:00:19.457
When the same event must be understood consistently across systems, timestamptz is usually the safer model.

00:00:19.457 --> 00:00:22.367
Choose temporal types based on meaning.

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:25.522
DATE is for calendar dates without time of day.

00:00:25.522 --> 00:00:30.207
TIMESTAMP stores a date and time without a time-zone interpretation.

00:00:30.207 --> 00:00:36.497
TIMESTAMPTZ represents an instant in time and is usually safer for events that cross regions or

00:00:36.497 --> 00:00:38.211
daylight-saving changes.
